-- title:
--   Theorem 7 (Whole Sequence Convergence): the IALM sequence converges to a local minimizer of (2)
-- statement:
--   Let $\lambda>0$ and $\mu>0$. Suppose that Assumptions 1, 2 and 5 hold, that is, $f:\mathbb R^p\to\mathbb R$ is $l_f$-smooth and strongly convex and $A$ has full row rank, and that the parameters are chosen as in (64) and (65). If $\{(w^k;u^k;z^k;v^k)\}_{k\in\mathbb N}$ is a sequence generated by IALM satisfying the stopping criteria (32), then there are $w^*,u^*,z^*$ such that
--
--   1. $\lim_{k\to\infty}(w^k;u^k;z^k;v^k)=(w^*;u^*;z^*;w^*)$;
--   2. $(w^*;u^*;z^*)$ is a P-stationary triplet of (2), with the constant $\alpha=1/\rho$;
--   3. $(w^*;u^*)$ is a local minimizer of (2).
--
--   This is the main result of the paper: a convergence guarantee for the whole sequence, for a method applied to a discontinuous and NP-hard problem, and it applies to the support vector machine, multi-label classification and maximum rank correlation models when the data matrix has full row rank.
--
--   Differences from the source:
--   - generalization: a sequence generated by IALM, whose primal step is computed by 0/1-BALM (Algorithm 2) → every sequence satisfying (32a), (32b), (33) and vᵏ⁺¹ = wᵏ⁺¹ with positive tolerances; reason: every 0/1-BALM sequence satisfies these relations, and the proof in the paper uses only these relations
--   - generalization: Assumption 2 with γ := √θ_min(AAᵀ) > 0 → any γ > 0 with γ‖z‖ ≤ ‖Aᵀz‖ for every z; reason: the paper’s γ satisfies this inequality, so the printed statement is the instance γ = √θ_min(AAᵀ), and the proof uses Assumption 2 only through this inequality
--   - generalization: (w*; u*; z*) is a P-stationary triplet, that is, (27) holds for some α > 0 → (27) holds with α = 1/ρ; reason: the proof gives (80) with the constant α = 1/ρ of the algorithm, and this implies the existential form of Definition 2
--   - encoding: A ∈ ℝⁿˣᵖ and its transpose Aᵀ → a continuous linear map between Euclidean spaces and its adjoint; reason: the same objects in the standard bases
--   - encoding: local minimizer of (2), a notion the paper does not spell out → feasible, with least objective among feasible pairs satisfying ‖w − w*‖² + ‖u − u*‖² < δ²; reason: the standard notion for a constrained problem, with the Euclidean ball of p.4
-- source:
--   Zhang & Xiu, Global Convergence of Inexact Augmented Lagrangian Method for Zero-One Composite Optimization, arXiv:2112.00440v1, Theorem 7, p.25

import Mathlib
import Definitions.Def_ZeroOneIALM_Assumptions
import Definitions.Def_ZeroOneIALM_Parameters
import Definitions.Def_ZeroOneIALM_Run
import Definitions.Def_ZeroOneIALM_LocalMinimizer
import Definitions.Def_ZeroOneIALM_PStationary

open Filter Topology

namespace ZeroOneIALM

/-- Theorem 7 (Whole Sequence Convergence), Zhang & Xiu, Global Convergence of Inexact Augmented
Lagrangian Method for Zero-One Composite Optimization, arXiv:2112.00440v1, p.25: under Assumptions
1, 2 and 5 and the parameter choices (64), (65), a sequence generated by IALM satisfying the
stopping criteria (32) converges to some `(w*; u*; z*; w*)`, where `(w*; u*; z*)` is a P-stationary
triplet of (2) and `(w*; u*)` is a local minimizer of (2).

**Formalization Note.** The sequence is any sequence with the relations of `IsIALMRun`, not only
one produced by 0/1-BALM. Assumption 2 is `IsRowRankConstant`. Definition 2 asks for some `α > 0`;
the conclusion records the constant `α = 1/ρ` given by the proof. -/
theorem theorem_7 {p n : ℕ} {f : EuclideanSpace ℝ (Fin p) → ℝ}
    {A : EuclideanSpace ℝ (Fin p) →L[ℝ] EuclideanSpace ℝ (Fin n)}
    {b : EuclideanSpace ℝ (Fin n)} {lam μ ρ lf γ η : ℝ} {ε : ℕ → ℝ}
    {w : ℕ → EuclideanSpace ℝ (Fin p)} {u z : ℕ → EuclideanSpace ℝ (Fin n)}
    {v : ℕ → EuclideanSpace ℝ (Fin p)}
    (hlam : 0 < lam) (hμ : 0 < μ)
    (h1 : IsSmoothWith f lf) (h2 : IsRowRankConstant A γ) (h5 : IsStronglyConvex f)
    (hpar : IsParameterChoice μ lf γ ρ η ε)
    (hrun : IsIALMRun f A b lam μ ρ ε w u z v) :
    ∃ (wstar : EuclideanSpace ℝ (Fin p)) (ustar zstar : EuclideanSpace ℝ (Fin n)),
      Tendsto (fun k => (w k, u k, z k, v k)) atTop (𝓝 (wstar, ustar, zstar, wstar)) ∧
      IsPStationaryWith f A b lam (1 / ρ) wstar ustar zstar ∧
      IsLocalMinimizer f A b lam wstar ustar := by sorry

end ZeroOneIALM
